17:17.320 --> 17:18.440
You might have to search forever.

17:19.300 --> 17:23.580
The universe is forcing you to keep the tape running forever, holding on to the entire history

17:23.580 --> 17:26.960
of the universe just to calculate a single binary value.

17:28.000 --> 17:33.360
What's fascinating here is how elegantly this mathematical model separates two concepts we

17:33.360 --> 17:34.420
normally conflate.

17:34.420 --> 17:39.520
We usually assume that if a system requires you to look deep, deep into the past, it must

17:39.520 --> 17:42.280
have a massive, complicated internal state.

17:42.460 --> 17:42.640
Right.

17:42.780 --> 17:45.600
Like, it must be remembering a million different variables.

17:46.080 --> 17:51.400
But the even process mathematically proves that an infinite memory depth can hide behind

17:51.400 --> 17:53.520
a trivial two-state system.

17:54.000 --> 17:58.540
It's like having a password to a vault that's just a single letter, A or B.

17:58.540 --> 17:59.940
The answer is small.

