But what happens if we use our projected classical description?

26:24.020 --> 26:27.280
What if we try to compose the probabilities instead of the amplitudes?

26:27.660 --> 26:27.980
Uh-oh.

26:28.600 --> 26:29.380
Let's trace that.

26:30.120 --> 26:35.860
The classical projection of a Hadamard gate is a matrix, where every transition simply has a 50-50 probability.

26:36.480 --> 26:36.760
Okay.

26:36.940 --> 26:46.060
So if I start with a 1, and I pass it through my projected tool, the tool says you now have a 50% chance of 0 and a 50% chance of 1.

26:46.060 --> 26:46.540
Right.

26:46.940 --> 26:51.180
Now, mathematically compose that projected probability matrix with itself.

26:51.620 --> 26:54.940
Apply that 50-50 classical blur twice in a row.

