What does classical probability theory tell you will happen?

26:58.260 --> 27:08.140
Well, classical probability says if I flip a coin to get a random result, and then I use that result to flip another coin, I just end up with a random result.

27:08.560 --> 27:12.380
50% of 50% of 25, plus 50% of the other 50.

