It all just washes out to a flat 50-50 blur again.

27:16.520 --> 27:16.920
Precisely.

27:16.920 --> 27:17.360
Okay.

27:17.360 --> 27:24.580
If you track classical probabilities instead of quantum amplitudes, you get the wrong physical answer when you sequence events together.

27:24.580 --> 27:25.120
Wow.

27:25.120 --> 27:33.280
The real universe perfectly restores the state back to 1, but your projected classical math predicts maximum uncertainty, a 50-50 blur.

27:33.280 --> 27:35.720
However, the composition completely fails.

