So if we throw away this vital phase information, if nature forces us to squash the 3D reality into a 2D probability, and we try to predict the future anyway, does that lost data just vanish into the ether, or does it leave a ghost in the machine?

29:17.780 --> 29:35.260
It absolutely leaves a ghost. And mathematically, that ghost is the kernel. The unobserved information, the quantum coherences, the lost phases, the invisible depth of your 3D object, acts as a mathematical entity that literally reaches back in time.

