The equation requires an instantaneous term, yes, but it also strictly requires a memory term.

29:59.440 --> 30:02.300
This memory kernel is an integral over past times.

30:02.300 --> 30:12.680
It records the effect of the observed state from previous moments in time, passing through the unobserved, hidden subspace, swirling around in the phase, and coming back to influence the present.

30:13.220 --> 30:19.940
So the shadow on the wall doesn't just act like a normal shadow. It acts like a shadow that remembers what shape it was three seconds ago.

