It just cares if the probability is mathematically greater than zero.

31:49.100 --> 31:49.980
Is it on the menu?

31:50.320 --> 31:50.840
Yes or no.

31:51.100 --> 31:56.700
Okay, so if I flip a coin, support sufficiency is just knowing that it can land on heads or tails.

31:57.240 --> 32:00.480
It could be a perfectly fair coin or it could be a horribly rigged coin.

32:00.960 --> 32:02.420
Support sufficiency doesn't care.

