And probabilistic sufficiency?

32:07.180 --> 32:09.940
That is the much harder standard to meet.

32:10.760 --> 32:15.340
Probabilistic sufficiency requires you to know exactly how likely each outcome is.

32:15.740 --> 32:17.900
You need the exact probability distribution.

32:18.380 --> 32:24.780
So probabilistic sufficiency is knowing that it's a rigged coin that lands on heads exactly 99% of the time.

32:25.020 --> 32:25.500
Precisely.

32:25.920 --> 32:30.640
And in Chapter 9, the manuscript proves something beautiful about the quantum state in relation to this.

