It tells you exactly how to carry a vector or a quantum phase or a piece of information smoothly and legally from state X to state Y.

34:56.240 --> 34:59.880
Okay, so a connection is basically the shipping instructions for the universe's data.

35:00.520 --> 35:03.080
Keep this box upright while moving it from Monday to Tuesday.

35:03.280 --> 35:04.280
That's a great way to put it.

35:04.280 --> 35:09.260
But the manuscript emphasizes something called holonymy, specifically in Chapter 25.

35:09.840 --> 35:11.320
What exactly is holonymy?

35:11.780 --> 35:16.960
Holonymy is what happens when you take your data on a road trip, travel in a loop, and come back home.

35:17.240 --> 35:23.860
You take a piece of data, you transport it along a path through space or time that eventually returns exactly to where you started.

35:24.140 --> 35:25.400
Okay, so I'm back where I started.

35:25.780 --> 35:27.060
Your base state is identical.

35:27.060 --> 35:38.460
You are back at location X, but because of the intrinsic curvature and geometry of the space you walked through and the rules of the connection you followed, the transported data has shifted.

35:38.880 --> 35:39.880
Wait, it shifted?

35:40.200 --> 35:40.380
Yeah.

35:40.560 --> 35:41.840
Even though I'm back in the same spot?

35:42.060 --> 35:42.360
Yes.

35:42.900 --> 35:48.680
The vector you are carrying has mysteriously rotated or acquired a phase shift compared to the moment you left.

35:49.160 --> 35:51.540
That geometric shift is the holonymy of the loop.

35:51.960 --> 35:53.640
Okay, I think I need an analogy here.

35:53.840 --> 35:54.460
Let me try this.

35:54.460 --> 35:57.880
Imagine I am holding a bowl of soup, right, filled to the brim.

35:58.600 --> 35:59.680
Okay, I'm with you.

35:59.860 --> 36:00.420
A bowl of soup.

36:00.620 --> 36:03.800
And I am standing on a specific tile on the floor of my living room.

36:04.580 --> 36:05.540
I start walking.

36:05.900 --> 36:07.760
I walk up a twisting spiral staircase.

36:08.120 --> 36:09.920
I walk across the upstairs landing.

36:10.320 --> 36:11.760
I take a left turn down a hallway.

36:12.400 --> 36:18.820
And then I walk back down a different spiral staircase, eventually stepping onto the exact same tile in my living room where I started.

36:19.120 --> 36:20.700
Right, the exact same base state.

36:20.700 --> 36:24.620
My base state, my physical location in the house, is 100% identical.

36:24.620 --> 36:33.320
But because of the complex 3D path I took, all those left turns and right turns and vertical climbs, the soup has sloshed and rotated inside the bowl.

36:33.500 --> 36:33.820
Naturally.

36:34.160 --> 36:41.760
I am in the exact same spot, but the orientation of the soup inside the bowl has changed based entirely on the geometric path I took.

36:42.380 --> 36:44.280
The soup's rotation is the holonymy.

36:44.280 --> 36:48.020
That is an exceptionally good visceral analogy.

36:48.240 --> 36:49.700
It maps perfectly to the math.

36:50.340 --> 36:54.620
In differential geometry terms, the base manifold is the floor of your house.

36:55.240 --> 37:01.220
The fibers of the bundle are all the possible ways the soup can be oriented above any given spot on the floor.

37:01.560 --> 37:02.160
And the connection.

37:02.700 --> 37:08.580
The connection is the laws of gravity and inertia, dictating exactly how the soup moves as you take each step.

37:08.580 --> 37:14.360
You return to the identical base point, but the fiber data, the soup's orientation, has transformed.

37:14.820 --> 37:19.820
Okay, I love the analogy, but wait, this raises a massive red flag for me.

37:20.100 --> 37:20.580
What's up?

37:21.000 --> 37:30.820
If the universe alters the data when it travels in a loop, if the soup sloshes around, doesn't that mean the universe is irreversibly destroying information?

37:31.300 --> 37:32.320
Why would it be destroyed?

37:32.320 --> 37:37.300
Because if the soup slosh is in the bowl, I can't easily undo that slosh.

37:38.000 --> 37:39.220
The friction dissipates it.

37:39.640 --> 37:43.200
If the quantum phase shifts, haven't we lost the original pristine state?

37:43.760 --> 37:45.640
Doesn't holonymy equal erasure?

37:46.300 --> 37:50.600
That is exactly the cynical intuition the manuscript anticipates.

37:50.920 --> 37:53.660
And it firmly, mathematically refutes it.

37:54.140 --> 38:00.320
In Proposition 26.3, Flyxion proves that non-trivial holonymy does not imply erasure.

38:00.320 --> 38:02.520
Really? How is that possible?

38:02.840 --> 38:04.800
If the data's changed, how is it not lost?

38:05.140 --> 38:09.360
Because parallel transport, mathematically, is a perfectly invertible operator.

38:09.520 --> 38:10.080
Invertible?

38:10.300 --> 38:10.680
Yes.

38:11.140 --> 38:14.440
The inverse transport always, always exists.

38:14.760 --> 38:25.680
If you walk your path backwards, exactly in reverse, up the down staircase, backwards across the hall, down the up staircase, the connection perfectly unwinds the shift.

38:25.900 --> 38:26.320
So it unsloshes.

38:27.140 --> 38:28.820
It perfectly unsloshes.

38:28.820 --> 38:32.020
Distinct input vectors remain distinct after transport.

38:32.160 --> 38:33.980
They never merge into a single point.

38:34.660 --> 38:36.240
The information isn't lost to the void.

38:36.440 --> 38:37.620
It is perfectly retained.

38:37.760 --> 38:40.940
It's just encoded as a geometric phase.

38:41.140 --> 38:41.280
Ah.

38:41.740 --> 38:45.200
Like the Pancharatnam-Berry phase in quantum mechanics.

38:45.340 --> 38:45.700
Exactly.

38:46.420 --> 38:50.120
The geometric phase is an explicit physical instance of this math.

38:50.120 --> 38:59.200
The quantum ray returns to its starting point, but parallel transport retains a complex phase associated with the global geometric properties of the path it took.

38:59.340 --> 38:59.940
That's incredible.

38:59.940 --> 39:04.500
The information about the entire journey is flawlessly stored in that relative phase.

39:04.500 --> 39:09.200
So the universe isn't a sloppy soup carrier tripping over its own feet.

39:09.200 --> 39:17.620
It's a flawless, frictionless machine that rigorously and mathematically encodes the exact history of the journey into the orientation of the soup.

39:17.840 --> 39:18.320
Precisely.

39:18.320 --> 39:27.800
And this geometric framework leads Flyxion to one of the most concrete striking examples in the text, which is the cubit triangle spanning chapters 11 and 29.

39:28.300 --> 39:28.580
Oh, yes.

39:29.020 --> 39:34.460
The author looks at the problem of trying to glue together local observations into a single global picture.

39:34.660 --> 39:35.500
The gluing obstruction.

39:36.160 --> 39:36.400
Right.

39:36.400 --> 39:39.860
Explain this triangle for me, because this blew my mind.

39:40.540 --> 39:42.780
Imagine three different experimental setups.

39:43.400 --> 39:46.360
Three measurement contexts for a single quantum bit.

39:47.040 --> 39:49.420
Let's call the contexts X, Y, and Z.

39:49.560 --> 39:49.780
Okay.

39:50.220 --> 39:57.400
The manuscript looks at what happens if you try to make these three contexts mutually unbiased using only real numbers.

39:57.400 --> 40:10.800
Now, mutual unbiasedness means that if you know with 100% certainty that the cubit is in a definite state in context Z, you have exactly a 50-50 chance of measuring either outcome in context X.

40:11.120 --> 40:13.660
They are maximally ignorant of each other.

40:14.240 --> 40:16.780
Total perfect uncertainty between the bases.

40:17.120 --> 40:20.620
If I know Z perfectly, I know absolutely nothing about X.

40:20.860 --> 40:21.120
Right.

40:21.420 --> 40:26.240
Now, you sit in your lab, and you observe the transition probabilities between Z and X.

40:26.240 --> 40:27.700
They are 50-50.

40:28.500 --> 40:30.680
You observe the transition between X and Y.

40:31.240 --> 40:32.220
Also 50-50.

40:32.640 --> 40:34.460
And between Y and Z.

40:35.160 --> 40:36.380
Also 50-50.

40:36.920 --> 40:37.180
Okay.

40:37.620 --> 40:38.320
Simple enough.

40:38.860 --> 40:51.120
You are a classical physicist, so you say, I want to build a global mathematical model, a frame assignment, using real numbers that respects all three of these local transition rules simultaneously.

40:51.120 --> 40:58.200
Okay, so I'm trying to build a single 3D object that perfectly casts all these specific 2D shadows I just measured.

40:58.500 --> 40:58.820
Exactly.

40:59.280 --> 41:07.160
But theorem 29.1 and proposition 29.2 prove that over the field of real numbers, this is mathematically impossible.

41:07.720 --> 41:11.080
It is a fundamental, inescapable geometric obstruction.

41:11.480 --> 41:12.200
But why?

41:12.760 --> 41:14.240
Why can't I just stitch them together?

41:14.720 --> 41:15.720
It seems so simple.

41:15.720 --> 41:17.120
Because of holonomy.

41:17.980 --> 41:32.320
If you try to transport a reference frame along the edges of this triangle, from context Z to context X to context Y and then back to context Z, the strict rules of those 50-50 transition probabilities force the frame to mathematically rotate.

41:32.540 --> 41:33.540
Because of the path.

41:33.920 --> 41:34.180
Yes.

41:34.180 --> 41:41.140
When you complete the cycle and arrive back at Z, the mathematical product of those transitions is not the identity matrix.

41:41.360 --> 41:43.460
It is not a perfect return to the original frame.

41:43.780 --> 41:44.580
The soup sloshed.

41:44.800 --> 41:46.340
The soup sloshed wildly.

41:47.140 --> 41:50.820
The cycle product is a rotation by an odd multiple of pi over 4.

41:51.120 --> 41:53.120
It's a rotation of 135 degrees.

41:53.740 --> 42:00.140
You physically cannot have a consistent global frame assignment if the cycle product doesn't return to the identity.

42:00.480 --> 42:00.860
Wow.

42:00.860 --> 42:06.720
So, the obstruction isn't a missing minus sign or a calculation error by the physicist.

42:07.500 --> 42:14.280
It's a fundamental geometric impossibility to flatten the universe's data without accounting for the path taken.

42:14.620 --> 42:15.560
You just can't do it.

42:15.680 --> 42:24.800
You literally cannot build a globally consistent real number model of this simple three-part triangle because the geometric holonomy of the universe explicitly forbids it.

42:24.920 --> 42:25.980
That's the brilliance of it.

42:25.980 --> 42:32.140
Over the complex numbers, you can do it, which is precisely why quantum mechanics is forced to use complex amplitudes.

42:32.460 --> 42:34.940
The complex phase absorbs the holonomy.

42:35.560 --> 42:40.440
But the obstruction itself is a profound structural property of how physical histories carry distinctions.

42:40.440 --> 42:58.160
Okay, my brain is buzzing, but if geometry and holonomy don't automatically destroy information, if parallel transport is perfectly invertible, and the universe is flawlessly keeping track of everything in these hidden phases and bundle fibers, then we are left with a massive glaring mystery.

42:58.340 --> 42:58.760
What's that?

42:58.760 --> 43:03.300
Where does actual irreversible information loss come from?

43:04.200 --> 43:07.080
If nothing is lost, why do we age?

43:07.500 --> 43:09.520
Why can't we unburn a piece of wood?

43:10.020 --> 43:12.800
Where does the arrow of time come from?

43:13.500 --> 43:15.940
This is the crux of part five of the manuscript.

43:16.520 --> 43:18.360
Flyxion confronts this directly.

43:18.360 --> 43:25.500
And the author makes a very strong, very precise claim that challenges a lot of standard thermodynamic thinking.

43:25.700 --> 43:26.240
What's the claim?

43:26.960 --> 43:33.160
Irreversibility is often just a loss of sufficiency in our description, not in the underlying physics.

43:33.860 --> 43:35.720
Wait, let me process that.

43:35.780 --> 43:38.260
The universe isn't forgetting we are.

43:38.920 --> 43:41.660
The physics is reversible, but our math isn't.

43:41.660 --> 43:42.340
Exactly.

43:42.780 --> 43:48.660
The manuscript introduces Proposition 30.2 to demonstrate this concept with painful mathematical clarity.

43:49.460 --> 43:55.900
Imagine a deeply simple, totally deterministic dynamic system, a function that just counts forward by one.

43:56.580 --> 43:58.280
f of n equals n plus one.

43:58.680 --> 43:59.200
Simple enough.

43:59.380 --> 44:04.300
It takes state one to state two, state two to state three, state negative five to state negative four.

44:04.800 --> 44:07.700
Okay, that is totally 100% reversible.

44:07.700 --> 44:12.860
If you tell me the current state is 10, I know with absolute certainty that the past state was nine.

44:13.240 --> 44:15.120
No information is lost in that dynamic.

44:15.260 --> 44:15.460
Perfect.

44:16.280 --> 44:19.060
Now, introduce a human observer to the system.

44:19.660 --> 44:23.620
This observer has a specific, slightly flawed measuring tool.

44:24.020 --> 44:25.000
A bad camera again.

44:25.200 --> 44:25.800
Sort of.

44:26.180 --> 44:28.220
The tool tracks negative numbers normally.

44:28.700 --> 44:30.840
If the state is negative two, it reads negative two.

44:31.260 --> 44:34.300
But for any positive number, the tool just logs a zero.

44:34.920 --> 44:36.420
That is the observation map.

44:36.420 --> 44:40.620
Okay, so if the true state is negative two, the tool reads negative two.

44:40.980 --> 44:44.100
If the true state is five, the tool reads zero.

44:44.680 --> 44:47.600
If the true state is 100, the tool reads zero.

44:47.860 --> 44:49.280
It's blind to positive integers.

44:49.900 --> 44:50.160
Right.

44:50.920 --> 44:53.920
Now watch what happens to the dynamics when viewed through this tool.

44:54.380 --> 44:56.720
The underlying universe goes from negative one to zero.

44:56.960 --> 44:59.480
The tool reads negative one, then it reads zero.

44:59.660 --> 44:59.960
Okay.

44:59.960 --> 45:02.720
The underlying universe goes from zero to one.

45:03.180 --> 45:05.600
The tool reads zero, then it reads zero.

45:06.080 --> 45:07.760
The universe goes from one to two.

45:08.200 --> 45:09.900
The tool reads zero, then zero.

45:10.420 --> 45:12.260
Oh, wow.

45:13.340 --> 45:14.800
Okay, I see where this is going.

45:15.020 --> 45:20.320
From the perspective of the recorded description, the state zero keeps transitioning to the state zero.

45:20.320 --> 45:26.060
But ask yourself, if you look at the tool and it reads zero right now, what was the past state?

45:26.760 --> 45:28.480
I have absolutely no idea.

45:29.040 --> 45:30.020
It could have been negative one.

45:30.420 --> 45:31.140
It could have been zero.

45:31.520 --> 45:32.580
It could have been 500.

45:33.020 --> 45:33.500
Exactly.

45:34.280 --> 45:38.080
Multiple unique pasts have collapsed into one indistinguishable present.

45:38.080 --> 45:41.060
The description has become logically irreversible.

45:41.400 --> 45:51.660
The observer has totally lost the ability to reconstruct the past, even though the underlying physics, f of n equals n plus one, is perfectly, flawlessly reversible.

45:52.580 --> 45:56.360
So information about the past was not destroyed by the universe's dynamics.

45:56.940 --> 45:59.720
It was destroyed by the compression of the description.

46:00.320 --> 46:00.560
Bingo.

46:00.980 --> 46:02.100
It's like a rigged roulette wheel.

46:02.100 --> 46:10.560
Imagine a roulette wheel that is totally mechanically rigged to land on green 80% of the time and red 20% of the time.

46:11.060 --> 46:12.480
Okay, so it has a clear bias.

46:12.800 --> 46:13.060
Right.

46:13.560 --> 46:15.300
It has a very clear bias, very clear direction.

46:15.480 --> 46:17.900
Over time, it is overwhelmingly moving toward green.

46:18.640 --> 46:21.160
But your observation tool is broken.

46:21.820 --> 46:23.120
It doesn't tell you the color.

46:23.680 --> 46:26.980
It only tells you if the number the ball landed on was even or odd.

46:26.980 --> 46:32.200
Oh, this leads perfectly into example 31.2 in the manuscript, the biased cycle.

46:32.680 --> 46:34.240
Your roulette analogy is spot on.

46:34.500 --> 46:35.480
Let's trace it physically.

46:36.040 --> 46:41.700
Imagine a random walk system that steps forward 80% of the time and steps backward 20% of the time.

46:41.940 --> 46:42.180
Okay.

46:42.460 --> 46:44.400
It has a massive rate of entropy production.

46:44.860 --> 46:47.980
It has a crystal clear, undeniable arrow of time.

46:48.260 --> 46:50.520
It is overwhelmingly marching in one direction.

46:50.740 --> 46:50.940
Right.

46:50.940 --> 46:56.820
If you stand back and watch it for a minute, you know exactly which way time is flowing because the particle is rapidly moving to the right.

46:57.520 --> 47:00.060
But now apply your rigged observation tool.

47:00.500 --> 47:03.020
The observer cannot see the exact position on the grid.

47:03.600 --> 47:06.280
The observer's tool only tracks the parity.

47:06.900 --> 47:11.020
Is the current state an even number or is it an odd number?

47:11.760 --> 47:12.060
Okay.

47:12.480 --> 47:13.180
Let's track the logic.

47:13.840 --> 47:18.740
If it's on an even square and it moves forward one step, it goes to an odd square.

47:18.740 --> 47:24.320
If it's on an even square and it moves backward one step, it also goes to an odd square.

47:24.860 --> 47:25.100
Yes.

47:26.060 --> 47:33.420
Every single physical step, whether it is an 80% chance forward or a 20% chance backward, fundamentally changes the parity.

47:33.920 --> 47:36.640
So what does the observer actually see printed on their ticker tape?

47:36.980 --> 47:41.200
The observer just sees a sequence that goes even, odd, even, odd, even, odd.

47:41.280 --> 47:43.140
It's just a perfectly alternating sequence.

47:43.620 --> 47:44.760
It looks like a metronome.

47:45.300 --> 47:46.540
And here is the kicker.

47:46.540 --> 47:51.340
What happens if you take that recording, even, odd, even, odd, and you play it in reverse?

47:51.860 --> 47:54.120
What is the time reversal of that sequence?

47:54.400 --> 47:59.700
It's odd, even, odd, even, which statistically is exactly the same alternating pattern.

48:00.080 --> 48:02.500
It's completely indistinguishable from the forward direction.

48:02.880 --> 48:03.260
Boom.

48:03.840 --> 48:08.600
The coarse entropy production of the observed data is exactly zero.

48:08.600 --> 48:14.360
The observer, because they are only tracking parity, sees a completely reversible process.

48:14.860 --> 48:17.400
The arrow of time has entirely vanished.

48:17.860 --> 48:18.280
Wait, wait, wait.

48:18.620 --> 48:23.700
Are you saying that if the observation tool is bad enough or compresses the wrong way,

48:24.160 --> 48:28.240
we could literally fail to notice the arrow of time passing right in front of us,

48:28.720 --> 48:30.780
even if the universe is rapidly aging?

48:30.780 --> 48:34.340
The manuscript mathematically proves this is a structural reality.

48:34.920 --> 48:41.300
The bias cycle has a strong objective direction, but an observer who records only parity cannot

48:41.300 --> 48:42.980
mathematically detect it.

48:43.640 --> 48:49.160
And Flyxion goes further to quantify this limit using theorem 35.1, calculating something

48:49.160 --> 48:52.100
called the Stein exponent of the arrow of time.

48:52.300 --> 48:53.520
The Stein exponent.

48:54.160 --> 48:57.240
I vaguely remember Stein's lemma from statistics.

48:58.020 --> 49:00.400
This is about hypothesis testing, isn't it?

49:00.400 --> 49:02.780
It is exactly about hypothesis testing.

49:03.180 --> 49:06.060
Imagine I hand you a VHS tape of a physical process.

49:06.500 --> 49:11.680
Your job is to watch the tape and guess, is this recording playing forward or is it playing

49:11.680 --> 49:12.160
in reverse?

49:12.660 --> 49:12.900
Okay.

49:13.340 --> 49:18.320
The Stein exponent measures the absolute maximum mathematical rate at which your confidence

49:18.320 --> 49:22.300
in detecting the true direction of time grows as you collect more data.

49:22.300 --> 49:27.640
And the theorem proves, unequivocally, that this detectable arrow of time is strictly,

49:27.640 --> 49:32.040
permanently limited by the observer's specific mathematical channel.

49:32.560 --> 49:38.440
So, the arrow of time isn't some global, absolute glowing beacon of truth that shines

49:38.440 --> 49:41.200
through everything in the universe regardless of how you look at it.

49:41.800 --> 49:44.980
It is entirely relative to the observation channel.

49:44.980 --> 49:51.020
As the author bluntly states, it is mathematically meaningless to ask whether a process has an

49:51.020 --> 49:55.240
arrow of time without explicitly specifying what is being observed.

49:55.600 --> 50:01.420
You can have a physical process with a pronounced massive arrow at a fine-grained level of description

50:01.420 --> 50:04.400
and absolutely zero arrow at a coarser one.

50:04.400 --> 50:07.780
This completely upends how I think about entropy.

50:08.620 --> 50:11.860
In pop science, we always hear, entropy always increases.

50:12.120 --> 50:13.220
It's the law of the universe.

50:13.360 --> 50:13.540
Right.

50:13.580 --> 50:14.340
It's the catchphrase.

50:14.340 --> 50:19.340
But what this math is saying is that the apparent entropy production, the actual irreversibility

50:20.060 --> 50:25.120
we experience day to day, is bounded by our own sensory and instrumental limitations.

50:25.980 --> 50:30.100
We are paying the memory debt of our own biological and mechanical course grading.

50:30.100 --> 50:30.620
Yes.

50:31.220 --> 50:36.760
And if we take a breath and scale this idea up, if the arrow of time and the growth of

50:36.760 --> 50:42.280
entropy can be completely masked by a limited local observation, what happens when we apply

50:42.280 --> 50:45.040
this math to the ultimate observation?

50:45.420 --> 50:45.800
Oh boy.

50:46.340 --> 50:50.520
What happens when we point our telescopes at the entire expanding cosmos?

50:51.000 --> 50:55.000
Which brings us to the final massive summit of our deep dive today.

50:55.000 --> 51:01.920
Part 7 of the manuscript takes all of these rigorous proofs about channels, memory debt, and sufficient

51:01.920 --> 51:06.380
observations, and hurls them at the scale of the universe itself.

51:07.000 --> 51:09.100
It's a huge leap, but a necessary one.

51:09.840 --> 51:15.540
The central conceptual distinction Flyxion makes here is between physical structure and

51:15.540 --> 51:16.660
accessible structure.

51:16.780 --> 51:16.920
Okay.

51:17.240 --> 51:18.460
Let's define those carefully.

51:19.000 --> 51:19.800
What's the difference?

51:19.800 --> 51:25.500
Physical structure is what is actually objectively out there in reality.

51:26.000 --> 51:31.720
It's the actual distribution of galaxies, the true quantum state of the vacuum, the objective

51:31.720 --> 51:33.620
variations in cosmic density.

51:34.140 --> 51:34.180
Okay.

51:34.320 --> 51:35.600
So it's the raw truth.

51:35.880 --> 51:36.100
Yes.

51:36.740 --> 51:42.820
Accessible structure, on the other hand, is only what a specific observer, bounded by a specific

51:42.820 --> 51:48.640
realistic measurement channel, can actually detect and statistically distinguish from a smooth,

51:48.640 --> 51:50.100
featureless background noise.

51:50.600 --> 51:54.980
So if the universe is a book, the physical structure is the actual text printed on the

51:54.980 --> 51:55.300
pages.

51:55.760 --> 52:01.060
The accessible structure is what I can actually read while looking through a foggy, scratched

52:01.060 --> 52:02.900
up pair of binoculars from across the room.

52:03.280 --> 52:03.840
Precisely.

52:04.300 --> 52:07.740
And this leads to what the manuscript terms the smoothness paradox.

52:08.540 --> 52:09.580
The paradox is this.

52:10.280 --> 52:15.400
A universe that is physically, actively forming complex structures like gas clouds condensing,

52:15.400 --> 52:21.120
galaxies grouping into massive clusters, stars igniting, might actually appear increasingly

52:21.120 --> 52:24.620
smooth and featureless to a bounded observer living inside it.

52:25.260 --> 52:25.500
Hold on.

52:25.580 --> 52:26.540
I need to push back on that.

52:27.080 --> 52:28.000
How is that possible?

52:28.620 --> 52:34.020
If the universe is literally getting clumpier and more complex, shouldn't my telescope see

52:34.020 --> 52:34.840
it getting clumpier?

